######## SETUP — transit topology + QoS enabled ########
QoS enabled globally: `mls qos enable` (prompts "Traffic will stop while configuration
is applied. Continue? (y/n)" - answered y+CR). Stack UNAFFECTED: both members Ready,
Operational Status "Normal operation", VMAC 0000.cd37.0d6f retained.
CoS lives in the 802.1Q tag, so the untagged access ports of 38394 could not show it.
Reconfigured to a TRANSIT path with tagged egress:
    vlan3010 "qos-transit" : port1.0.1(t)  port2.0.1(t)   both trunk, native vlan none
    tb470 eth2 <-> port2.0.1 (member 2 = MASTER)
    tb470 eth3 <-> port1.0.1 (member 1 = BACKUP)
    rx/tx VLAN offload disabled on eth2+eth3 so 802.1Q tags survive capture
Driven as a pure L2 test - tcpreplay injects tagged frames on the wire, tcpdump reads
them off the far side - so Linux IP routing cannot shortcut between tb470's two NICs.
Traffic: 10.10.10.1 = MATCH source, 10.10.10.2 = NO-MATCH source, both sent at prio 0.

######## CONTROL — no policy applied ########
  02:00:00:00:00:01 ... vlan 3010, p 0 ... 10.10.10.1.1000 > 10.10.10.99.2000
  02:00:00:00:00:02 ... vlan 3010, p 0 ... 10.10.10.2.1000 > 10.10.10.99.2000
=> Both sources transit the stack and arrive with p 0. Any later CoS change is
   therefore the policy acting, not a pre-existing marking.

